Appendix B. 1D Travelling Wave Analysis: Complete Rigorous Asymptotics

We present the full matched asymptotic expansion that establishes the existence of a saddle‑node bifurcation (fold) of travelling waves in the limit of high activation energy. The analysis is formal but systematic; it can be made rigorous by classical methods of geometric singular perturbation theory (Fife 1979, Berestycki–Nicolaenko–Scheurer 1985).

B.1 The flame‑sheet limit \varepsilon \to 0

The dimensionless system in 1D, with w = 0 after a Galilean shift into the front frame, is

\frac{1}{\mathrm{Pe}} \Theta'' + c \Theta' - \mathrm{St} \, \Theta + \lambda \Psi(\Theta) \Upsilon = 0, \qquad c \Upsilon' = \beta \Psi(\Theta) \Upsilon,

with \Theta(\pm\infty) = 0, \Upsilon(+\infty)=1, \Upsilon(-\infty)=Y_b. The reaction function is \Psi_\delta(T) = \frac12(1+\tanh\frac{T-\bar T}{\delta}) e^{-T_{ac}/T}. We consider the distinguished limit \delta \to 0 (sharp ignition temperature) and T_{ac} \to \infty with

\varepsilon = \frac{T_\infty^2}{T_{ac} \Delta T_c}

as the small parameter (inverse of the Zel’dovich number). The ignition temperature T_c corresponds to \Theta = 1 in dimensionless units. Then, for \Theta < 1, \Psi is transcendentally small; for \Theta > 1, it is exponentially large. The reaction is confined to a thin layer around \Theta = 1.

