Appendix D. Singular Value Degeneracy at the Fold: Detailed Linear Algebra

We prove the assertion about the condition number of the Fisher matrix near a fold.

Setup. Let \boldsymbol{\theta} = (s, \mathbf{u}) with s the dangerous parameter, \mathbf{u} \in \mathbb{R}^{p-1}. The forecast map near the critical manifold s=0 is

\mathcal{F}(s,\mathbf{u}) = \mathcal{G}(\mathbf{u}) + \mathbf{v} s^2 + O(s^3),

with \mathbf{v} \notin \operatorname{range}(D\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{u})). The Jacobian is

J(s,\mathbf{u}) = \begin{pmatrix} D\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{u}) & \mathbf{0} \end{pmatrix} + 2s \mathbf{v} e_1^{\mathsf T} + O(s^2),

